# Backend Testing

Activate `laravel-best-practices` skill → `rules/testing.md` for factories, fakes, and assertions.

Run tests inside Docker — see `docker` rule.

Framework: **PHPUnit** classes (`php artisan make:test --phpunit {Name}`). Do not add Pest.

## Test layers

| Layer | Location | Covers |
|-------|----------|--------|
| **Service** | `tests/Unit/Services/{Name}/{Name}ServiceTest.php` | Every **public** method on `{Name}ServiceInterface` / `{Name}Service` |
| **Feature** | `tests/Feature/` | HTTP: auth (401/403), validation (422), JSON status — not every service edge case |
| **Support/helpers** | `tests/Unit/` | Pure PHP without HTTP (e.g. `TranslationHelper`) |

Business logic lives in services — **service tests are mandatory** for new or changed services.

## Service test requirements

When adding or changing `app/Services/{Name}/`:

1. Create or update `tests/Unit/Services/{Name}/{Name}ServiceTest.php`
2. **Every public method** on the service interface must have at least one test
3. Add separate tests for failure paths and edge cases where behavior differs (not one test per method only — cover meaningful branches)
4. Resolve the service via **`{Name}ServiceInterface`** (validates DI binding):

```php
$service = $this->app->make(OfferServiceInterface::class);
```

5. Do **not** test private or protected methods directly
6. Do **not** test pass-through controllers — test the service instead

### Dependencies

| Dependency | Approach |
|------------|----------|
| Another `*ServiceInterface` | Mockery mock → `$this->app->instance(Interface::class, $mock)` |
| Database / Eloquent | `LazilyRefreshDatabase` + factories (add the trait on the test class) |
| Mail, Queue, Events | Fakes (`Mail::fake()`, `Event::fake()`) **after** factory setup |

### Example structure

Illustrative only — names are placeholders, not existing classes:

```php
namespace Tests\Unit\Services\Offer;

use App\Services\Offer\Contracts\OfferServiceInterface;
use App\Services\Offer\Dto\CreateOfferDto;
use Illuminate\Foundation\Testing\LazilyRefreshDatabase;
use PHPUnit\Framework\Attributes\Test;
use Tests\TestCase;

class OfferServiceTest extends TestCase
{
    use LazilyRefreshDatabase;

    #[Test]
    public function create_persists_offer(): void
    {
        $offer = $this->app->make(OfferServiceInterface::class)->create(
            new CreateOfferDto(title: 'Flat downtown', price: 100_000),
        );

        $this->assertModelExists($offer);
        $this->assertSame('Flat downtown', $offer->title);
    }
}
```

Service tests that need the container or Eloquent must extend `Tests\TestCase` (not bare `PHPUnit\Framework\TestCase`).

### Assertions

- Prefer `assertModelExists()`, `assertSame()`, `assertNull()` over raw `assertDatabaseHas()` when asserting models
- Use factory **states** instead of manual attribute overrides where states exist
- Prefer descriptive test names: `create_rejects_negative_price`

## Feature tests

- One feature test file per HTTP area (e.g. `tests/Feature/Offers/OfferStoreTest.php`)
- Cover: guest/auth 401/403, successful request, validation errors
- Avoid duplicating every service edge case — that belongs in `{Name}ServiceTest`

## Running tests

Agents may run tests **without asking first**:

```bash
# Changed service
docker compose exec -T php php artisan test --compact tests/Unit/Services/Offer/OfferServiceTest.php

# Single test
docker compose exec -T php php artisan test --compact --filter=create_persists_offer

# All unit / feature
docker compose exec -T php php artisan test --compact --testsuite=Unit
docker compose exec -T php php artisan test --compact --testsuite=Feature

# Full check (lint + stan + tests)
docker compose exec -T php composer test
```

After service changes, run the matching service test file before finishing.

## Checklist for new service methods

- [ ] Public method added to `{Name}ServiceInterface` and `{Name}Service`
- [ ] Binding in service provider
- [ ] At least one test per public method in `{Name}ServiceTest`
- [ ] Edge/failure tests for non-trivial branches
- [ ] Feature test updated only if HTTP contract changed
